    "TRANSCRIPT SHAPE: 510 lines, 0:00:06–0:44:51, header «83% سطریں ملیں», no «- خلا:» line. Teacher's own page numbers: «صفحہ نمبر ہے 2056» (0:00:09), «صفحہ نمبر 2057 پہ دوسری لائن» (0:05:37), and paragraph pointers «اگلے صفحے پر دیکھیں» (0:38:43), «دوسرے پیراگراف» (0:38:52), «تیسرے پیراگراف» (0:39:44), «آخری پیراگراف» (0:40:48) — not used as book pages. Malformed stamp «[ 43:28]» (line 490) — not used. One Devanagari word «रोकना» inside 0:27:43 (transcription artefact for «روکنا»). English loanwords in the teacher's speech («بائی ڈیفالٹ», «ڈکلیئر», «آنورڈ», «یونینز») are his own. No model chatter or repeated drafts. Several ع: lines carry the same stamp as the next Urdu line (e.g. 0:18:05–0:18:08, 0:20:28–0:20:31, 0:24:22–0:24:24) — whisper alignment compresses the read-through; used as they are. 0:15:37 line comes before 0:15:41 though its content is long (alignment).",
